## What to run
Run each of the 7 samples individually via `run_samples.sh <Sample>` (so one failure does not mask
the others), record exit code, duration, final PASS/completed marker. If a sample fails, re-run it
once to record determinism. Then run the aggregate `run_samples.sh` once.

## Classify every failure
(A) DONTWAIT/backpressure, (B) terminal/error classification, (C) known pre-existing (name the prior
evidence `file:line` in `doc/plan/c016-worklog/*.md` — e.g. D-084 .NET Gateway state-lane finding in
`decisions.ko.md`), (D) environment/runner, (E) binding-port dependency. Verify (C) by exact
assertion, not counts. Capture the first failing assertion/log excerpt with `file:line`.

